92186297041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6c24d250-c966-5806-b13d-89fc68943e50" :question/math-academy-id "q-316593" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9eb3ccd040b0a8bca45f30780e62bd77fdd3333005e748ad40d47afc20f82ea4.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(3+3)\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-6\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc6d2c22-82b3-53ad-b113-cae12dc34407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296257}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296257} :answer-field/id #uuid "260ae894-6d7c-5be2-a23c-69bf76d7518d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ef63fda8-672c-521f-acf1-a12cdcd6d118" :question/math-academy-id "q-316595" :question/problem "![](images/54/54537b6712dc9ae74b8b65cd0a14d5d3e878709ae35b2fc5701c7b1a6dd6d044.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(5+2)\\cdot 2=7.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-3)\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 0=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-9\\,|\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3277d0fd-3830-5b78-8ece-5b6fba39df58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295551}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295551} :answer-field/id #uuid "a63ea200-97e5-5687-a63f-50b70b4429bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cd7e4493-a7b6-54d3-aa1d-1fe94b70e848" :question/math-academy-id "q-316597" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c8048c789a15d2cfbcdbabce65d256ba1bcda14bc4a02067a2ef9f2287e0656.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}=9\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-5\\,|\\cdot 9\\pi  \\\\  & =45\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50b013a9-6fe1-5bd7-8678-418477c1b397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295731}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295731} :answer-field/id #uuid "e31ced79-29bb-51e0-bd1e-36dc299e5d0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c03ca7c8-c82e-584d-94ea-e6bf67face17" :question/math-academy-id "q-316598" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](images/68/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-4)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 1=-12-2=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-14\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id