nswer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331938} {:answer/id #uuid "fd6c096c-bf7b-5938-80e6-6115d33f998f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$f(x)$ does not have any local maxima" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331938} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1f3ab1c-7d13-5548-8d07-8bdc6170269a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56c5438a-da5f-5788-885e-7f027b595c02" :question/math-academy-id "q-49024" :question/problem "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{x}$ defined for $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ have a local maximum?" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}{ln}^{2}⁡(10)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ on $(0,\\infty )$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)} & =0 \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡x & =1 \\\\ x & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=e$ is a stationary point. Next, to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=1,{e}^{2}$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{(1)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}({e}^{2}) & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{(e)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}=-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(0,e)$ | $e$ | $(e,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $1$ |  | ${e}^{2}$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n- At $x=e,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=e$ is a local maximum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=e.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4020acf4-04e1-5b60-a2f7-a157b1314764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x{log}_{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330520} {:answer/id #uuid "731eefef-20d5-574f-9043-1000fa8c1ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330987} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4ee1b1-d9b2-51c6-abc3-dc91b813f3ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x{log}_{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331379} {:answer/id #uuid "c509c861-23e4-5b8d-8b8d-1044b852afdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331700} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2baf64-fef0-5fb3-8a66-3f57f615f35a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331761}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331700} :answer-field/id #uuid "497ee4c0-825b-5385-b6b4-603172d90ac7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a0b5476f-0e78-5366-afe4-a0704f4f9240" :question/math-academy-id "q-49051" :question/problem "![](images/22/22505181ad0a10e74a158edabc949444055f1deda57286ff63674c32f2dc79c7.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ on the curve $y={log}_{2}⁡x$  that is closest to the origin (as shown above) satisfies the equation \n\n$$\n2x+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAAA}}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the *squared* distance $S$ between $(0,0)$ and a general point $P(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x,y) & =(x-0)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe require that the point $P$ lies on the curve $y={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the minimum distance, we take the first derivative of $S(x)$ and equate it to zero. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x)=2x+2{log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "009d8131-2ffe-5c14-a378-d1f56781bded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{x}+2ln⁡(K|x|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329958} {:answer/id #uuid "3c89723c-b495-521d-8ad7-e34b357b5559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x}+2ln⁡(|K|x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330487} {:answer/id #uuid "7a074152-9317-5da0-b3eb-342d5c464ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+2ln⁡(|K|x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331032} {:answer/id #uuid "a03000cf-9b4c-5aa7-bc81-3a390be00d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{x}+ln⁡(2K|x|)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331391} {:answer/id #uuid "e71d945d-91e1-5744-9e87-32bc4829e8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+(1+ln⁡(K|x|))^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331980}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329958} :answer-field/id #uuid "47f28b39-da74-5b7f-b9d6-861abb2e2dcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "edf6e555-e835-5bc6-9e0b-944e25006b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-49067" :question/problem "What is the antiderivative of ${(1+\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(1+\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+2ln⁡|x|+\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{-2+1}+C \\\\  & =x+2ln⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant $C,$ we can always write $C=2ln⁡K$ where $K$ is some other positive constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with $2ln⁡|x|$ term, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(1+\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =x-\\frac{1}{x}+2ln⁡|x|+2ln⁡K \\\\  & =x-\\frac{1}{x}+2(ln⁡|x|+ln⁡K) \\\\  & =x-\\frac{1}{x}+2ln⁡(K|x|).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ea8d40-84bf-534f-8e8c-6302589f6d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2xln⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330280} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4ddb04-2a0f-541d-8c66-b81a1140bf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "ln⁡|2-\\frac{1}{x}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330472} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecd5285-27bd-58a2-ae63-f8d42089b197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-ln⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331373} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfcaae4-3cd8-5b37-ad78-afba74998213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x-4ln⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332021} {:answer/id #uuid "f6fa8737-41d4-5415-b503-7159707db2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{(2x-ln⁡|x|)}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332021} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a2c34fc-7951-5002-8305-c48283de9967" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3c37bd55-c0e8-559f-80d9-e5fdbb837ece" :question/math-academy-id "q-49100" :question/problem "Find the integral of ${(2-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}$ with respect to $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(2-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x-4ln⁡|x|+\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{-2+1}+C \\\\  & =4x-4ln⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332661 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64328e68-62e1-53dd-9cfb-7398eb993288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{csc}x-2\\operatorname{cot}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330842} {:answer/id #uuid "8aeb842f-aeaa-5e41-b067-5daed501c3d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}x+2\\operatorname{tan}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331183} {:answer/id #uuid "a3677c87-1d81-51dd-8a89-966172c275aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csc}x-2\\operatorname{sec}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331413} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c429dd-3478-55e6-b756-94a76a605818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{csc}x-2\\operatorname{tan}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331704} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4bb0d0-92fa-5871-a2d8-fc85d9224fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{sin}^{3}x-2\\operatorname{cot}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331771}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330842} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0820439-91be-5bbd-bf0c-17495c4b5b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b36d025f-bace-58ef-adb7-3885184b511c" :question/math-academy-id "q-49121" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int csc⁡x(3cot⁡x+2csc⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-cot⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int csc⁡xcot⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-csc⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int csc⁡x(3cot⁡x+2csc⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3csc⁡xcot⁡x+2{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 3csc⁡xcot⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int csc⁡xcot⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(-csc⁡x)+2(-cot⁡x)+C \\\\  & =-3csc⁡x-2cot⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332662 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274362a6-a3c6-5920-81f8-1b2abcf16ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{tan}x+4\\operatorname{csc}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330301} {:answer/id #uuid "4a02aa3a-212d-52ee-bcdb-e1c48e5f318d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{tan}x-4\\operatorname{csc}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330616} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5434a6-e354-57cc-8be3-921a471e1964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{tan}x+4\\operatorname{sec}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330929} {:answer/id #uuid "c85ca58b-0676-50a2-a51f-81c36b63f586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cot}x+4\\operatorname{sec}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331724} {:answer/id #uuid "eeff4377-3048-5370-9c27-9dad4e9d4466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cot}x-4\\operatorname{sec}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332047}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330929} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5cb83ec-ba9e-5744-a1c6-b0f47594acda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c3a5d5fb-8f22-572d-9122-04a2c3a1b6ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-49122" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int sec⁡x(7sec⁡x+4tan⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =sec⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =tan⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int sec⁡x(7sec⁡x+4tan⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (7{sec}^{2}⁡x+4sec⁡xtan⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 7{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 4sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7tan⁡x+4sec⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46505b2f-1953-51c1-89b1-262c3e1e114f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\text{ arcsec }x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330584} {:answer/id #uuid "53ca920a-4368-56bd-b725-1abcf2b6713e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330708} {:answer/id #uuid "61645379-6ba4-5686-88be-a9d0c67ea769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330813} {:answer/id #uuid "927c467d-2be8-5aa7-9b42-5199a503c166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\text{ arcsec }x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331254} {:answer/id #uuid "a6184f98-47c2-57d1-922d-d6ecf85d4ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\text{ arcsec }x-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331435}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330584} :answer-field/id #uuid "9269b8e4-4637-529d-ad83-2e10b9866149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93133dfc-bc5a-589b-9b21-0d9909f27fa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49136" :question/problem "If ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\text{ arcsec }x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83244f3f-d4c0-5400-b575-23be5005ae8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331114} {:answer/id #uuid "af9bdfa5-e153-5f0e-9579-128cbb842449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{2}⁡3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331502} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b54574-c597-5d2e-b623-f716b57a4a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332087} {:answer/id #uuid "faa172fc-7c4f-5556-9b0f-aa9ceeebb1f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332150} {:answer/id #uuid "fbfd483a-4f6a-531f-b6bb-82a660adeb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332164}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332164} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d0ff93-0be5-5775-8d8d-a9a9d7becf1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "80f918c1-b02c-51df-b3e3-2c8413bacd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-49256" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10304a96-adfd-5511-8b38-70b4e4cb2215" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330091} {:answer/id #uuid "6da2efe0-b31d-592f-96a9-1b37aaf477e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330932} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e3fa5a-567a-51e0-bc36-1958095f5813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331682} {:answer/id #uuid "dc447439-382c-515e-b293-790fca1f2316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331901} {:answer/id #uuid "f47329b5-6d59-5ad4-b066-1dc0b16cbbc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332103}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330932} :answer-field/id #uuid "70002cb7-bb15-57f9-b1f8-e67051228ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2e2d21ac-046c-5274-bb89-c9bfaff5e9df" :question/math-academy-id "q-49257" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}{|}_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b95828-a685-54a8-96b4-b52ae657e912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330153} {:answer/id #uuid "444fa90c-41cd-594e-acf1-cfca43d9f868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330563} {:answer/id #uuid "4e61c48b-d79c-5d63-9602-758c8c834289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330664} {:answer/id #uuid "7f11ee4d-4f0b-51c9-8e3d-549f4a158d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331072} {:answer/id #uuid "89b1ee96-afb9-5e02-a824-2992fac6b5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331175}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330563} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f414d51-cc19-5057-95ed-395de2e5b540" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f3ad6824-baa3-5500-876c-87beb97cf8ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-49277" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}+C \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{-1}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38ab7134-266a-55b0-8dd9-092f7793e4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330457} {:answer/id #uuid "75ef0166-fd95-54fe-b5df-525ead63381c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331008} {:answer/id #uuid "95684c85-1b97-54e9-97fb-b17ebcc31860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331275} {:answer/id #uuid "d81e6757-4b9f-56b0-99e6-30d04faf2681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331866} {:answer/id #uuid "e3374bc6-ffec-53a1-9944-f67c29759f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{tan}^{2}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331957}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331275} :answer-field/id #uuid "89d8ab03-5e24-50d3-bb4c-13c096f28d48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "73bdd419-9ea0-5251-ace5-0e2f286a0252" :question/math-academy-id "q-49280" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\n$$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c5821ad-3d4f-57c6-a299-5d7eb8eb6393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330643} {:answer/id #uuid "9313388c-be46-561d-9054-618eddeb5792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331257} {:answer/id #uuid "968b5dbc-fc14-52e1-b8ba-c858af9d76e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331286} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf4b03b-f1c8-5d81-b6e3-2abcf9f93640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331617} {:answer/id #uuid "fd662dda-2335-5bcb-a678-23c74459f46b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332176}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331286} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ced3b9-575e-546e-8f36-c27932699fb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c693f81-0fae-5be2-839f-6622073dd810" :question/math-academy-id "q-49281" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let  $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48b77ad6-2790-5fb9-ac75-c531ab004c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330601} {:answer/id #uuid "8a571c79-fa20-5257-bd99-b3a3310b2bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331178} {:answer/id #uuid "8b31c3cf-dd75-5df7-9b83-aa025a1ed598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331185} {:answer/id #uuid "9549f7ba-8509-55bb-ac17-34f5f78e130c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331274} {:answer/id #uuid "d75920df-cc3f-5f99-8620-29d4802abe07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330601} :answer-field/id #uuid "075617b4-7fd7-5fe0-bba2-6157b32a856f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a78f750a-573a-57da-b09b-e012074904df" :question/math-academy-id "q-49284" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\n$$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332694 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25b0850f-fa25-5b05-9950-7e0e634c06c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330275} {:answer/id #uuid "61fe0262-2ac7-5c54-8be0-54f9f416208b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330827} {:answer/id #uuid "6a515304-6a32-5abe-a406-870f9a6a8691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330905} {:answer/id #uuid "82b1f11b-9dc9-5745-9d60-f88f832c5e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331105} {:answer/id #uuid "e429182d-57f1-592c-ae86-682900ce93a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331962}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331105} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ee28e4-2550-58c8-bf71-43555f4f9c46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a41d63bd-84eb-5f5c-b954-12d95e773df1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49286" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f8e4dc1dff5673d8fc95375f9632f43bc4942335899e0e6dad11e8693bd6599.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=5{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi .$ The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=5{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi $ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}([\\pi -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )]-[0-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11dbbe25-f605-5318-ad46-dc495bb13c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330105} {:answer/id #uuid "ab70ca2b-b076-587e-a88e-1d10fb8a7498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331469} {:answer/id #uuid "bf37637a-7683-56c4-bb69-925e9cc147a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331645} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d35bf0-51c8-56cd-8c8d-1bcbce77b9af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331802} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ef6fe2-0740-5343-acd8-b64c29efd3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330105} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0499ae3-ea01-5507-9906-ec2b8d72e827" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "489c69ce-d415-5c5f-8b91-c246b0512a1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49294" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dcc78643dd44633f778d954de32a955dc5803abf7dc059c30bbbda97bc35413f.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x & ={cos}^{2}⁡x+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }[\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi +3\\pi )-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\pi +\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027c7b2d-b6da-57b7-bebe-fb4037a57c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi (8\\pi +1)}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329986} {:answer/id #uuid "5edb996b-f64a-5b21-a842-f045e68a17ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\pi }^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330794} {:answer/id #uuid "694123a1-c921-511a-acce-7bbd45a25a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11{\\pi }^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330892} {:answer/id #uuid "992e5b44-a5b7-5d52-9616-a516782a146b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi (3\\pi -2)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331319} {:answer/id #uuid "c067d35b-09ff-52a9-b0d8-b519ceb90554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331656}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331319} :answer-field/id #uuid "518cab6c-8aef-56e1-9322-1acdbcc19ee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e50b0ecc-a7e1-5f2d-884d-81b7bbf09d3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-49299" :question/problem "![](images/20/20844131c3d35b02f0ba7c6567b7765a54f0909e63ee309181dd5a25248dbfd5.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1=-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-x+{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\pi +{\\pi }^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{{2}^{2}}] \\\\  & =-\\pi +{\\pi }^{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}-4\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}+2\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3\\pi -2)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "387deba6-304f-5fb3-b47c-69364ee68fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330456} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbd38f5-b598-5f41-b8e7-6a2e96e2e92b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331363} {:answer/id #uuid "d53e8abf-0959-5a9c-839c-8502bcc230cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331839} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d621ba-aeb4-5686-b23c-d3e8132c191b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332066} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f51ac7-9c9e-5857-be9f-ae4d9ff5c99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332143}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332066} :answer-field/id #uuid "650973e6-7b74-5955-b3e6-7ccc008e872e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "22c49d6a-442c-592d-b81d-9330777b0cac" :question/math-academy-id "q-49325" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are using the identity\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{3(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008298da-bf7a-51ca-837d-ab329d0489ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329955} {:answer/id #uuid "099d6ddf-d5f2-5fd1-9989-6721d1ea7bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330034} {:answer/id #uuid "88ac8b32-2829-5bde-aed3-69f279dfedfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331164} {:answer/id #uuid "97b2c286-d293-598e-8173-52cb4aaa72e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331301} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c3c459-f04c-5677-8215-e3b74b9824f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331681}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331681} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2910a34-30ac-5541-b445-de1db206308c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d70cb193-c0f3-511e-a986-3ca7b8cef3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-49332" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0860c1d8-216d-5466-9f62-ccae7b52e912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330020} {:answer/id #uuid "203a6ea8-eba0-5d40-aa09-a59a360ffbdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330226} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb98399-a9d4-5fe9-bc96-644e80f830a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330488} {:answer/id #uuid "823db0e7-2377-5017-b419-f145d5d9961d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331099} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3e9f10-f5ea-57a0-9d29-03b20270bd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331177} :answer-field/id #uuid "a10a89c1-f082-55be-bb60-453abc8e5020" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "71ebda71-dbd6-53ac-9e9c-22ae8c3a8413" :question/math-academy-id "q-49446" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.$ \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}=\\frac{1}{-{sin}^{2}⁡x}=-{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26bff1d2-1a1f-5568-b606-c926ad4e222e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330288} {:answer/id #uuid "38f382b6-b9e0-5d37-bb15-bf2017958200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330460} {:answer/id #uuid "88b1a168-dccc-5c24-aa5c-58eef11e4b53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\text{arcsec}(4x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331165} {:answer/id #uuid "8a671a08-acf6-51a4-a4b1-a79a1a8a1a19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(16x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331179} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c62bda-b0cb-5477-843f-9e7f08c270e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331672}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331672} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ed515ce-b125-59ef-ba87-1982f7680cc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cd302e3c-b39d-509b-8801-010e64d93a57" :question/math-academy-id "q-49519" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{4|x|\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{4|x|\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|4x|\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $4x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{4|x|\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|4x|\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b0edf81-9914-5a0f-b9b6-d58d70540093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330630} {:answer/id #uuid "70cf07b2-a48c-5c20-b1ad-493648041c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(9x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330962} {:answer/id #uuid "9a56a3d4-f0db-5dee-8e1b-e1e7174dd979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331338} {:answer/id #uuid "a43c7a93-7056-56e0-adc4-8cc368c5eac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331423} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c453d1-3b22-5ee0-8261-9dc453f931aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331996}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331996} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3ccce72-f1f2-5395-8899-d57e02ead31c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "751e8889-464b-57e5-9446-01158bf809c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49554" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{3|x|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{3|x|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|3x|\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $3x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3|x|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|3x|\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1afb9d8c-3f67-5355-93d6-a9093bad7dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330187} {:answer/id #uuid "3226e3a9-ff07-580d-875b-1db26197856a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(36x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330391} {:answer/id #uuid "d697edf8-7533-5458-807b-5604ad7429ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331847} {:answer/id #uuid "d72cc629-030b-503a-b49e-63c0be8afa3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331853} {:answer/id #uuid "d885db49-c6b0-5c70-8dc4-c09546b4b009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(36x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331870}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331853} :answer-field/id #uuid "89604dd1-6f4e-5479-bb62-31a5924f3f5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8067bb84-25f1-5b9a-af1c-e522b42ac4cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-49555" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{6|x|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{6|x|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $6x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{6|x|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51a96887-12f9-54a7-9f27-889811c6585e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330691} {:answer/id #uuid "5be25893-006e-5120-bfc9-3385c633e5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x+1}{5}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330772} {:answer/id #uuid "8597e78d-6a6c-513d-99e9-421156a1013b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x+2}{5}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331136} {:answer/id #uuid "93c370e2-9cd9-5e58-a79b-66978cc6b8b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331260} {:answer/id #uuid "c88f3648-0e88-5c0c-930e-b5d8abbd6773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x+5}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331136} :answer-field/id #uuid "1358753c-7bf6-5eb8-b3a1-6471cbbf4b86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "85c37b78-e926-5fab-baa1-c0d49d07ba65" :question/math-academy-id "q-49689" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}-25 & =25[\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}-1] \\\\  & =25[{\\left(\\frac{x+2}{5}\\right)}^{2}-1]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{25[((x+2)/5)^{2}-1]}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\cdot \\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\cdot 5\\cdot \\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{15}{|x+2|\\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|(x+2)/5|\\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\frac{x+2}{5}.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+2}{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|(x+2)/5|\\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x+2}{5}\\right)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a39296-35ee-53cf-bfb8-6a10b78a1084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330379} {:answer/id #uuid "54c780ec-8ed0-59df-9662-49d663639bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330714} {:answer/id #uuid "d22501a3-a221-5893-92d1-782b53f97c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331815} {:answer/id #uuid "ee61e062-2a60-5418-91a5-bc857edab7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332044} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ebae5-f2cd-530f-bdd8-1769730a7359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332161}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330714} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba7992fb-af57-5bce-a970-c192ca7e1d84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9a51e949-edb8-581f-9b0d-82187677b8f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-49712" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(x){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e-x{|}_{1}^{e}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}(e-e+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332769 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3600375c-6616-5cea-9dbb-06d93d322153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330432} {:answer/id #uuid "4f160d4c-6ac6-5cb3-9501-4b70dae49244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330668} {:answer/id #uuid "874bf0d8-e732-5738-a6f8-43214bd49daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331158} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d1fbe3-8070-5dff-b33a-01d398ee45e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331411} {:answer/id #uuid "c89fa789-fa91-5256-b87a-54f50dc91609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331726}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331411} :answer-field/id #uuid "717b7e5f-5a3f-51d8-bc85-2eb60331d441" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "35ad8649-a1a5-5a33-9485-b718f80b516f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49727" :question/problem "What is the limit of the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡n}{n+2}$ for $n\\ge 1?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nWe calculate the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches at infinity,\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡n}{n+2}.\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡n}{n+2}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sequence converges,  and its limit is $0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a4eaf87-5ad7-5588-a8ca-b8e137778ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${c}_{n}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330179} {:answer/id #uuid "324e8469-c9c7-5503-91c1-aa058cb410b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${a}_{n}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330393} {:answer/id #uuid "86cf4341-391e-55b3-8fdb-e98fe5968d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${a}_{n}$ and ${b}_{n}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331150} {:answer/id #uuid "935473b9-48f4-59d8-b28b-491db7fa919f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${b}_{n}$ and ${c}_{n}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331258} {:answer/id #uuid "d714a245-fcdb-5169-8beb-958f334e5d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${b}_{n}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331852}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330393} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb6cbe08-9982-519d-b975-bf9d755be669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6e38da10-344b-5d2a-90f4-c2515d2ccf2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49734" :question/problem "Which of the following sequences, defined for $n>1,$ diverge?\n\n- ${a}_{n}=\\frac{n\\sqrt{n}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n)}$\n- ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(2n)}{{e}^{n}}$\n- ${c}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{5}}{{e}^{n}}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nTo find the limit of each sequence, we must evaluate them for $n\\to \\infty .$\n\nFor ${a}_{n}=\\frac{n\\sqrt{n}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n)},$ both the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nFor ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(2n)}{{e}^{n}},$ both the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{b}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFor ${c}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{5}}{{e}^{n}},$ both the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{c}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"${a}_{n}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "341bbdfc-0958-57c4-a8fc-adcfd2832b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330412} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4eb11e-164a-505d-8222-3a3c8cc2aa8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330473} {:answer/id #uuid "5173e85f-be65-57f7-b4ad-50a4243824a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330686} {:answer/id #uuid "900d9ce2-2884-5941-890f-cca5011570ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331231} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a39abd-a637-559d-b40e-9331517387e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331945}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331945} :answer-field/id #uuid "99a69d51-520e-57bf-a0e9-67ec91b1dca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "defadd51-e009-5740-8eb4-1acd4e92eb56" :question/math-academy-id "q-50018" :question/problem "A curve has parametric equations $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).$ Given that $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t),\n$$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t),\n$$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t))}{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡(2t)}{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{csc}^{3}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}{|}_{t=\\pi /12} & =-\\frac{1}{4}{csc}^{3}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{sin}^{3}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{3}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eee4af2-0248-5ce4-b7f6-6fee6d1a8fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330507} {:answer/id #uuid "662007e1-aa2b-54ce-b04c-f2ad08993265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330861} {:answer/id #uuid "6687452e-ac8c-536f-9456-54fd1b9619f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330866} {:answer/id #uuid "712abd91-42eb-5ec8-84bf-b6f634404a67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd3b07d-2774-58fa-93e9-db174c995ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331226}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330507} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d43db0b-4e5d-5721-97a5-e44ef07baae7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "830e243e-5841-5ab7-af4b-a130c74364b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-50409" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={sin}^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={cos}^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41aac7b0-e36a-52aa-883e-d2ddfd33ab74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330532} {:answer/id #uuid "5e338882-ec9b-52c8-9509-458d83a50da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330790} {:answer/id #uuid "8489b988-e5d3-5081-88ab-f63b44492691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331127} {:answer/id #uuid "f89ff7dc-52c8-5018-b8e3-07b4fec5c000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332135} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfbc103-aa8d-5079-8217-c29c118b141a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22c019a-4532-5eef-bb3c-f171fa627817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "90f83aed-c049-593e-9f58-73c0262de78f" :question/math-academy-id "q-50411" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{sec}^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{sec}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "590d6352-1cb2-5f07-b337-1a5ebbae468c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330748} {:answer/id #uuid "ab5d39fd-d361-5948-ac25-d41727644ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331468} {:answer/id #uuid "b88545d6-ff7b-56de-916f-9ba100472dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331581} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6a7743-731d-57fb-8d43-9d7442d6b434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332006} {:answer/id #uuid "fa786860-e6f1-53ee-9dfb-09fcd349a209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331581} :answer-field/id #uuid "18da3dd1-3b0e-5e20-8435-771e2e44e2a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "132c7e25-b8d1-5b60-bc80-45357d89a5d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-51126" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /24}({cos}^{2}⁡2x-{sin}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x={cos}^{2}⁡2x-{sin}^{2}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /24}({cos}^{2}⁡2x-{sin}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}{|}_{0}^{\\pi /24} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e030aa-17f5-575b-8c19-593762858129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329960} {:answer/id #uuid "010d087f-2168-5876-808a-6b8533f7c847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cot}^{4}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329963} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb829f0-81ef-56be-bafb-8ab19d120737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330222} {:answer/id #uuid "26f69ffa-f857-59e2-b56a-7e672ff829bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cot}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330293} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3c9b4b-592e-55d1-a295-2f8df0fe6364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+{sec}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330951} :answer-field/id #uuid "dec408f1-4e20-5669-b90f-578445063800" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c6b28878-fcf8-5c77-8f92-3c4ca2e564a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-51270" :question/problem "![](images/87/87dc32f8909ac1c05adc981b4133a3f6e721918e4aca6923b08a073d2fb8cfe9.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{3}],$ as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ $a=-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ and $b=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{1+{sec}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1040edda-0303-5346-ac49-2025a711486e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(1-x)ln⁡(10)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330092} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3385ec-93b4-59c7-a196-58be5d17d757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{(1-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330189} {:answer/id #uuid "430a86b3-46fa-5177-b8b1-9abf9afaa40a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(1-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330550} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2c3511-369b-5b02-8467-198f1bcf8279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1-x)ln⁡(10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330941} {:answer/id #uuid "afdc0472-7689-57f5-b5c2-148cb66217a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{ln⁡(10)}{(1-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331507}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330092} :answer-field/id #uuid "85a34950-0b5d-5d67-b7f8-2bcede974234" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0c643137-d804-5b6f-93e8-568de57f1d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-51317" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=log⁡(1-x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=log⁡u={log}_{10}⁡(u),\\,u=1-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(10)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(10)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)ln⁡(10)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1-x)ln⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0720f878-f9e6-57b7-a9ad-2cafdbf9fd46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csc}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330012} {:answer/id #uuid "60210d84-bcdd-576f-90af-4f4b4412e584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{csc}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330802} {:answer/id #uuid "6697d4e8-d25b-57a8-8cd4-582cc3f62c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330870} {:answer/id #uuid "9a34ba3f-6e5c-57fc-b2c0-b71cbd4bde90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{csc}^{3}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331333} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d5e7fb-cd5f-5e32-b78c-1ece3aded26d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡t}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331705}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331333} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb631b10-44cd-5de1-b74f-0fe092fa9f31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e1d829e6-cbc8-5156-8b9c-b8c7a64d3319" :question/math-academy-id "q-54157" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ Given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(3\\operatorname{cot}⁡t)}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{csc}^{2}⁡t}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =3{csc}^{3}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "033ef8e4-0132-5350-9528-79791d39157f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333016} {:answer/id #uuid "05706693-651e-5af5-88bc-7c7abc314b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333033} {:answer/id #uuid "073e778a-1825-51a2-9ad1-a82b274fb53c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=sin⁡x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333060} {:answer/id #uuid "0b38ae2d-e945-50a4-9fcf-a5b4c47bf27b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "5${sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta $" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333092} {:answer/id #uui